Subject: [PATCH] Find users by phone number and by @username

getUsersByPurpleName() understands two kinds of name: an "id<n>" buddy and
a display name. Anything else ends in "User not found", so a message or a
call addressed the way a phone dialer or an address book would address it
goes nowhere:

- a phone number, e.g. "+15555550100". TdAccountData already keeps a phone
  index (getUserByPhone), so look the number up there.
- a Telegram @username. Add TdAccountData::getUsersByUsername(), which
  matches case-insensitively, with or without the leading '@', against the
  editable username and every active username, and try it when no display
  name matches.

Display names still take precedence over usernames, so nothing that resolved
before resolves differently now.

This is the pull request as it stands after review, squashed; it takes in:
- ea8798c "Compare usernames as ASCII, leaving other bytes alone" (Mikhail T.)

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/UnitedMarsupials/tdlib-purple/pull/29]
